// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/igla/own_model.t27 -- the one map of "our own model": IGLA CODER, HSLM in t27, and the
; harness that has to run them. 27 cells, one T27F reel, the same workflow as the two topic reels
; (specs/t27f/reel_t27_basics.t27, specs/t27f/reel_gf16_nmse.t27): topic_engine.t27 decides each
; cell's status from what was measured, topic_reel.t27 checks it, reel.t27 and deck.t27 draw it.

; SOURCES, read on MEASURED_ON:
;   - gHashTag/igla-coder-gpu at CODER_COMMIT (private): README.md, LEDGER.md,
;     results/report_pair_10b.md, research/T27_BENCH.md, research/MODEL_ON_FPGA_PLAN.md.
;   - gHashTag/trinity at TRINITY_COMMIT: docs/experiments/FOUND_EXPERIMENTS_SUMMARY.md (the HSLM
;     experiment ledger) and data/wave9/worker-2/hslm_step_10000.bin (the one HSLM checkpoint left).
;   - gHashTag/trinity-training at TRAINING_COMMIT: src/hslm, 64 Zig files, the HSLM trainer.
;   - gHashTag/trinity-fpga at FPGA_COMMIT: 8 tokens on the AX7203, 7682304/7682304 receipts.
;   - gHashTag/t27 at SOURCE_COMMIT: the ML specs named per cell.

; MEASURED on 2026-10-17:
;   - test: t27c test-report (built from SOURCE_COMMIT, zig 0.16.0) on the Railway lab, 17 ML specs:
;     cross_entropy_loss 5/5, sgd 4/4, adam 4/4, lamb 4/4 pass, 0 vacuous. BLOCKED, never compiled:
;     nn/hslm (undeclared 'constants'), hslm/forward_pass ('q_role'), nn/attention
;     ('PHI_CUBED_INV'), optimizer/adamw ('allocate_array'), and all nine specs/igla/coder/*.t27.
;     ternary_matvec.t27 (the FPGA matvec, outside the 17) passed 4/4.
;   - re-test on 2026-10-18, same t27c, after the PR that rewrote both HSLM specs (#7778):
;     nn/hslm 26/26 and hslm/forward_pass 14/14 pass, 0 vacuous, so 6 of the 17 compile. The
;     spec's backward pass is now real, each gradient checked against a finite difference.
;     That spec was not the trained model: 6 layers at ctx 81, FFN 243-972-243 with GELU and no
;     embedding or vocab head, where trinity-training ran 3 blocks, its best run at ctx 27, and an
;     FFN 243-729-243 with ReLU, biases and a TWN scale.
;   - re-test on 2026-10-18, same t27c, after the PR that rewrote nn/hslm to the trained model
;     (#10062): nn/hslm 46/46 pass, 0 vacuous. It now has the trained shape (3 blocks, ctx 27,
;     phi position encoding and phi-RoPE, a ReLU FFN 243-729-243 with biases and TWN alphas, the
;     vocab-729 head and cross-entropy), its backward reaches the embedding, and every gradient is
;     checked against a central difference; a mutant that drops one alpha fails 10 of the 46.
;     Not in it then: the per-block VSA path, f32, and the trainer's STE update (shadow weights).
;   - re-test on 2026-10-18, same t27c, lab checkout brought to master, after the PR that gave
;     t27 a pure arena allocator and a file I/O contract (specs/ml/arena_heap.t27 10/10,
;     specs/ml/file_io_contract.t27 12/12) and rewrote optimizer/adamw (#10077): adamw 12/12
;     pass, 0 vacuous, its moment buffers carved from the arena. cross_entropy_loss 5/5, sgd 4/4,
;     adam 4/4, lamb 4/4, nn/hslm (61/61 after the VSA PR) and hslm/forward_pass 14/14 still pass, so 7 of the 17
;     compile. nn/attention ('PHI_CUBED_INV') and the nine coder specs stay BLOCKED. Cells 24 and
;     25 stay gaps: the arena and the file contract are specs of what t27c must lower, and t27c
;     lowers neither (no heap, no file I/O, no `--backend ml`; that work waits for the owner's
;     owner-approved-foreign label).
;   - re-test on 2026-10-18, same t27c, after the PR that made the IGLA CODER specs compile
;     (#10075), on top of the entry above: all nine specs/igla/coder/*.t27 compile and pass with 0
;     vacuous, so 16 of the 17 (only nn/attention is still BLOCKED). The padding tests that asserted
;     nothing (`verify baseline`, `assert true`, forall invariants that lower to NOT CHECKED) were
;     deleted, not counted. The specs now write into caller buffers (no allocator in t27c yet).
;     benchmark.t27 carries the t27 bench counts (466 items = 391 strict + 75 other, cell 4) and
;     eval.t27 the pass@k estimator and the report_pair_10b rows (cell 5), each with relation tests.
;   - test on 2026-10-18, same t27c, after the PR that added the training step (STE, backward, data):
;     nn/ternary_ste 26/26, nn/hslm_backward 15/15, nn/hslm_data 39/39 pass, 0 vacuous. The STE is
;     the TWN quantizer (delta 0.7 * mean abs, alpha = mean abs of the kept weights), the
;     pass-through gradient, clip_grad_norm and the SGD step on the shadow weights. hslm_backward
;     runs forward, backward, STE, clip, SGD and requantize on one 3-head slice of the model
;     (ctx 27, head_dim 3): its trit, bias and input gradients match a central difference to 1e-6
;     and 20 steps cut the loss below half. hslm_data holds the curriculum, next-token batches and
;     the MSLH header and layout, whose byte count equals hslm_step_10000.bin (4971796). Not in
;     them: the STE on the whole 3-block model, the tokenizer, shuffle; AdamW, heap and file I/O are in the entry above.
;   - re-test on 2026-10-18, same t27c, after the PR that added the VSA path: nn/hslm 61/61 tests
;     pass, 12 invariants proved, 0 vacuous. Each block now runs the VSA stream of model.zig
;     forwardTrain (bind, rotate, the PHI_INV gate, +0.1 * project(context) when it fires, the
;     output into the next block); the stream never reads a float parameter, so the gradient
;     checks hold with it on. A gate mutant (> for >=) fails 2 tests and a gain-0 mutant fails 1.
;   - re-test on 2026-10-18, t27c built from SOURCE_COMMIT, lab checkout at master ba78d6d3c, after
;     the PR that made nn/attention compile (#10094): nn/attention 35/35 pass, 9 invariants proved,
;     0 vacuous. The other seven re-run on the same checkout still pass (cross_entropy_loss 5/5, sgd
;     4/4, adam 4/4, adamw 12/12, lamb 4/4, nn/hslm 61/61, hslm/forward_pass 14/14), so 17 of the 17
;     ML specs compile and pass, and cell 23 has its passing test. The DELIVER cells' evidence was
;     re-taken on the same checkout for the review of that PR: nn/ternary_ste 26/26,
;     nn/hslm_backward 15/15, nn/hslm_data 39/39, ml/arena_heap 10/10, ml/file_io_contract 12/12,
;     0 vacuous (cells 16-18); playra/tern-tc-9m and tern-tc-9m-t27 200, tern-tc-100m 401 (cells 7
;     and 8); the board /state 200 (cell 21). A review of that PR is what the engine asks of cells
;     7, 16, 17, 18 and 27; REVIEWED turns true only in a later PR that names the approving review.
;   - test on 2026-10-18, t27c with `--backend ml` (#10165), lab checkout at master 8887f17f4:
;     ml/host_io_model 3/3 pass, 0 vacuous. `t27c compile specs/ml/host_io_model.t27 --backend ml`
;     builds a binary that exits 0 and leaves a real 24-byte /tmp/t27_tokens.bin (bytes 00000000
;     01000000 50c40000 ffffffff 07000000 78563412, sha256 48548924cac8...); with that path made a
;     directory the binary aborts, exit 134. So t27c lowers file I/O (Linux syscalls on a real fd)
;     and the arena of ml/arena_heap is plain t27 it already lowers: cell 24 has its passing test.
;     The backend builds that file-I/O program only; the training binary is the next entry.
;   - test on 2026-10-18, same t27c, lab checkout at master 2d358a708, after the PR that added
;     ml/train_slice_model (#10186): 5/5 pass, 0 vacuous. `t27c compile
;     specs/ml/train_slice_model.t27 --backend ml` builds a binary that runs 20 steps of the
;     nn/hslm_backward training step through `use` (loss 3.2975044 to 0.32346588), writes the trained
;     trits, biases and both losses to a 379-byte /tmp/t27_train_slice.bin, reads it back byte for
;     byte and exits 0; with that path made a directory it aborts, exit 134. So t27c lowers a model
;     spec to a training binary, for one 3-head slice; not for the whole 3-block model (cell 25).
;   - published on 2026-10-18: playra/tern-tc-100m on Hugging Face, the 100M ternary model of the
;     igla-coder-gpu ladder (n_layer 12, d_model 768), trained on RunPod; final.pt sha256
;     620c80b642ff87f06f945f6dbedf122e69fd524e93b7b20d1fd9bfcfd3d08300, both run summaries pinned
;     by sha256 in its model_card.t27 (14/14 on the lab). Validation bits per byte 0.4722 against
;     0.4217 for the fp twin of the same recipe: the ternary model is the worse of the two.
;   - live: GET huggingface.co/api/models/playra/tern-tc-9m, .../tern-tc-9m-t27 and
;     .../tern-tc-100m returned 200 (tern-tc-100m answered 401 before 2026-10-18).
;     GET board-production-2dec.up.railway.app/state returned 200 and a made-up path 404; its
;     live jobs include own_model since 2026-10-18 06:33 UTC, the event t27c gen-json makes from
;     specs/igla/own_model_board.t27 (it was stale since 2026-10-05 before that).
;   - review: #10164, #10179, #10186, #10185 and #10270 merged without one, each by auto-merge
;     before the reviewer bee had approved it (#10270 named REVIEW_ID_TBD and was taken back by
;     #10273). So this change, PR REVIEW_PR (below), puts the evidence of cells 7, 8, 16, 17, 18,
;     25 and 27 to review once more, with auto-merge off: review REVIEW_ID is the reviewer bee's
;     APPROVE of it. REVIEWED is true for those seven DELIVER cells and for no other cell.
;   - board on 2026-10-18, cell 26: specs/fpga/ddr3_head_bandwidth.t27 (11/11 tests, 0 vacuous on the
;     lab), lowered by t27b verilog around a LiteDRAM core, routed by openXC7 for xc7a200tfbg484-2 and
;     flashed on the AX7203 with openFPGALoader -c digilent_hs2. Its UART receipt: 325000 beats
;     (10,400,000 bytes, the head) read back in 375548 to 375554 clocks of 10 ns, M = 2769 MB/s
;     (86.5 percent of the 3200 peak, gate 2000), 0 bad beats, the read checksum equal to the write
;     checksum and to the value the spec's test predicts (FFB7236C398EE555), verdict PASS, the same on
;     a second flash. A mutant that checks each beat against the next beat's pattern reported
;     E = 325000 of 325000 and FAIL. Not closed: nextpnr puts the 100 MHz clock at 85 to 95 MHz, the
;     worst path inside the LiteDRAM core, and 3 of 9 routes pass the BIOS memtest; the receipt is
;     from those that do. This is a sequential read of a pattern, no weight on the board and no
;     compute from DDR3, so the cell is a draft at 10 percent, a DELIVER step waiting for its review.
;     Cell 26 has no review: its PR, #10248, merged without one, so it stays a draft.
; The engine asks an engineering LEARN step for a source link, a PRACTICE step for a passing test
; and a DELIVER step for a review. So: 3 published, 22 verified, 1 draft, 1 gap.

; PERCENT is a second, separate number per cell: an estimate of how much of that part exists, with
; its basis in SOURCES. It never feeds a status. The lens and overall figures are plain means, every
; cell weighted the same; that weighting is a convention, not a measurement.

; THE ANSWER this map gives: HSLM was trained before, in Zig only (64 files); its best runs
; (PPL 2.96 at ctx 27) were wiped by EXP-002 and survive only in the ledger. In t27 the loss, four
; optimizers and the HSLM spec's forward and backward passes pass, and that spec is now the trained
; model, its VSA path included (see MEASURED); the ternary STE, the training step and the data
; and checkpoint layout now pass too, on a model slice and on bytes; heap and file I/O are t27
; (ml/arena_heap, ml/file_io_contract, ml/host_io_model) and `t27c --backend ml` lowers them to a
; binary that writes a real file, and to a training binary for one head slice
; (ml/train_slice_model); the STE and a training binary over the whole model are not done. A 100M ternary model is public; nothing past 100M parameters is.

; Not claimed: no model quality beyond the numbers in SOURCES; no GIF or MP4, stills only.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

